;======================================
; THE BYZANTINE SHADOW
; MODULE 03 -- ECONOMY FOUNDATION
;======================================
;
; Pass 1 responsibility:
;   Establish a deterministic baseline gatherer allocation.
;
; Transactional production is NOT implemented here. The Pass 1
; transaction kernel owns capital feasibility, escrow, authority,
; execution, verification, and release.
;
;======================================

(defrule
    (unit-type-count-total villager < 30)
    (can-train villager)
=>
    (train villager)
)

; ============================================================
; BYZANTINE-GENERALIZATION (project policy, no donor analogue):
; villager count is capped at 30 so continuous TC production cannot
; silently drain the food/gold capital that transaction objectives
; (Feudal/Castle progression) require. 30 sits above the donor's
; Dark-age villager thresholds (FlushDarkAgeVills 23,
; KrushDarkAgeVills 29) so the opening is unaffected. Revisit when
; the Castle-age economy transition is transplanted.
;
; Gatherer percentages were briefly owned here (static 60/40 boot +
; Feudal gold rules) but are now owned by the authenticated donor
; machine in 03f_donor_gatherer_policy.per (100% food open, staged
; rebalancing incl. gold on dropsite proximity and Castle
; progression). Static rules removed 2026-09-17 to avoid competing
; writers on the same SNs.
; ============================================================
